---
# The page always has a step (Resize), so there is no deadlock to find;
# liveness is RequestsSettle.
deadlock_detection: false
---
# The project page (#/projects/<slug>) as the person sees it: the
# CLIENT-side state machine of web/src/project.tsx ProjectView +
# ProjectPage + ProjectHome + ProjectComposer, the MEMORY.md editor
# (web/src/orb.tsx FileEditor, mounted in the Project panel) and the orb
# status strip (project.tsx OrbLine). Recipe: go/tests/model/README.md.
#
# Where project_main_threads.fizz follows the server (Main's lock, the
# thread's report), this follows the screen: which column, drawer, rail,
# panel and dialog are up, what the composer and the editor are doing,
# and the server facts only where they change this page (main exists,
# one thread's group, main's orb).
#
# What is on screen, from the code:
# - Nothing but a status until the first GET /api/projects/{slug} lands:
#   <Pending what="Project"/>, or the ErrorNote with Retry when it
#   failed. A later failed poll keeps the detail and shows nothing (err
#   is read only while there is no detail), so it is not a step here.
# - view is ProjectView's `open`: "home" (""), "main" (detail.main) or
#   "thread" (the one modelled thread). The home is the composer, then
#   main's row and the threads by group; beside a conversation the
#   threads are a column at the left, folded to a rail when the person
#   folded it (remembered, bough:prj-threads-folded) -- only where it
#   is a column (wide).
# - wide is the viewport class: max-width:1080px is "tight", where the
#   thread column and the Project panel are drawers over the
#   conversation behind one scrim, and the rail and its chevron are not
#   drawn. (The <860px class changes only widths, nothing a person can
#   do, so it is folded into tight.)
# - panel is the Project panel. Its default is one remembered choice,
#   bough:prj-panel ("" unset, "0", "1"), written only by the Project
#   button at wide: unset, it is up on the home and down beside a
#   conversation. ProjectPage's effect on [tight, onThread] re-derives
#   it and closes the drawer whenever the viewport class changes or the
#   page goes between the home and a conversation (main <-> thread does
#   not flip onThread, so it keeps both).
# - composer is ProjectComposer on the home: "empty", "typed",
#   "sending" (textarea and Send disabled, "Sending..."), "failed" (the
#   error under it, the text kept). Enter sends, Shift+Enter is a
#   newline; typing is one step. A send that lands opens main
#   (onMessage: messageProject, load, setOpen(main)). Leaving the home
#   unmounts it, so its text goes with it.
# - files is the definition files read (GET /api/projects/{slug}/orb):
#   the editor waits on it, a failure says so with Retry.
# - mem is the MEMORY.md tab of FileEditor: "clean", "dirty" (a draft;
#   Save enabled, the tab wears a dot), "saving" ("Saving...", Save
#   disabled), "saved" (the "MEMORY.md saved." note, 2.6 s), "failed"
#   (the server's error beside the editor, the draft kept). The editor
#   lives in the panel: the panel going down unmounts it, and its draft
#   and a save's outcome go with it (see KNOWN GAPS).
# - orb is main's container as detail.mainOrb says: "none", "starting"
#   (starting/building; up is false until it runs), "running",
#   "stopped". The strip's words are strip(), its Stop link shows only
#   while orbUp. Stop asks first when main has running jobs
#   (confirmStopOrb): dialog is that modal, modelled with jobs running.
# - thread is the one thread's group (threadGroup): "none" (no thread,
#   or archived/moved: the stale-thread effect sends a page showing it
#   home), "running", "unseen" (Finished -- unseen), "done". The done
#   group starts folded in the column (CLOSED); done_folded is its head's
#   aria-expanded, inverted. Viewing an unseen thread acks it (the App's
#   viewingUnseen, one step here), and dropping it on Done does too.
#
# Scope cuts, since every generated path is one browser walk:
# - One thread, started by main's Start thread button (main stays on
#   screen). New thread, the project.yml parse error callout, the Show
#   all cap (>8 rows) and thread orbs add controls, not mechanisms.
# - No navigation while the composer is sending: an in-flight send
#   still opens main when it lands, wherever the person went.
# - The editor's Edit waits for the "saved" note to fade.
# - The main thread's own status (the column's main button) is the
#   conversation's business, not this page's.
# - The rest keep the graph near 450 states (442, 1499 transitions):
#   the files answer before the detail and only their first read fails;
#   only the first message fails; the page's work (messages, threads,
#   the orb, the editor) is walked on the wide page with the rail open
#   (busy_ok), the editor with nothing else moving (quiet), and while a
#   save answers or its note shows the person only closes the panel or
#   waits (still); main's orb stops only with no thread; the viewport
#   changes only on a quiet page before the panel choice is remembered;
#   the rail is folded and unfolded beside one conversation.

def overlay(p):
    # At tight the panel and the thread drawer cover the page behind a
    # scrim: nothing under it can be clicked.
    return (not p.wide) and (p.panel or p.drawer)

def column_shown(p):
    # The thread list beside a conversation: a column at wide unless
    # folded to the rail, a drawer at tight only while open.
    if p.view == "home":
        return False
    if p.wide:
        return not p.rail
    return p.drawer

def list_shown(p):
    # Somewhere a thread row can be clicked or dragged: the home's
    # queue, or the column/drawer beside a conversation.
    if p.detail != "loaded":
        return False
    if p.view == "home":
        return not overlay(p)
    return column_shown(p)

def thread_row_shown(p):
    # The column's done group is folded until opened; the home never
    # folds a group of one row.
    if p.thread == "none" or not list_shown(p):
        return False
    if p.view != "home" and p.thread == "done":
        return not p.done_folded
    return True

def still(p):
    # No modal up, and no save of MEMORY.md answering or just answered.
    # Scope: while a save is in flight or its note is up, the person
    # only closes the panel (the discard in KNOWN GAPS) or waits.
    return not p.dialog and p.mem not in ("saving", "saved")

def busy_ok(p):
    # Scope: the page's work (messages, threads, the orb) is walked on
    # the wide page with its files read and the rail open; the tight
    # page, the rail and a failed files read are walked around it.
    return p.wide and p.files == "loaded" and not p.rail and not p.dialog

def quiet(p):
    # Scope: the editor is walked with nothing else moving on the page:
    # no message in flight, main's orb settled, the thread at rest.
    return p.composer == "empty" and p.orb != "starting" and p.thread in ("none", "done")

def panel_wanted(pref, view):
    if pref != "":
        return pref == "1"
    return view == "home"

def panel_shown(p):
    return p.detail == "loaded" and p.panel

def strip(orb, main):
    # OrbLine's words, as the product says them: orbUp is status
    # "running" or up, and a starting/building orb is not up yet.
    if orb == "none":
        if main:
            return "Main thread has no orb yet."
        return "No orb yet."
    if orb == "running":
        return "Main thread's orb - Running"
    return "Main thread's orb is stopped."

def status_line(p):
    # The one thing that always says where the page is: the pending
    # line, the error, or the crumb (the slug and the counts on the
    # home, "All threads · <title>" beside a conversation).
    if p.detail == "loading":
        return "Loading project"
    if p.detail == "error":
        return "Couldn't read this project"
    if p.view == "home":
        return "counts"
    return "crumb"

role Page:
    action Init:
        self.detail = "loading"
        self.files = "loading"
        self.main = False
        self.view = "home"
        self.thread = "none"
        self.done_folded = True
        self.orb = "none"
        self.composer = "empty"
        self.wide = True
        self.pref = ""
        self.panel = panel_wanted("", "home")
        self.drawer = False
        self.rail = False
        self.mem = "clean"
        self.dialog = False

    # --- how the page's views go between each other ------------------

    atomic func settle(before):
        # ProjectPage's [tight, onThread] effect, run after any step that
        # changed the viewport class or moved between the home and a
        # conversation. The panel going down takes the editor with it.
        # Leaving the home unmounts ProjectComposer: its text goes too.
        onthread_changed = (before == "home") != (self.view == "home")
        if self.view != "home":
            self.composer = "empty"
        if onthread_changed:
            self.relayout()

    atomic func relayout():
        shown = self.wide and panel_wanted(self.pref, self.view)
        if self.panel and not shown:
            self.mem = "clean"
        self.panel = shown
        self.drawer = False

    atomic func close_panel():
        if self.panel:
            self.mem = "clean"
        self.panel = False

    # --- the first read and the files --------------------------------

    atomic fair action Loaded:
        # Scope: the files' first read answers before the detail's.
        require self.detail == "loading" and self.files != "loading"
        self.detail = "loaded"

    atomic action LoadFail:
        require self.detail == "loading" and self.files != "loading"
        self.detail = "error"

    atomic action Retry:
        # The ErrorNote's Retry: load() and loadFiles() again.
        require self.detail == "error" and still(self)
        self.detail = "loading"
        if self.files == "error":
            self.files = "loading"

    atomic fair action FilesLoaded:
        require self.files == "loading"
        self.files = "loaded"

    atomic action FilesFail:
        # Scope: only the first read fails (a retried one answers).
        require self.files == "loading" and self.detail == "loading"
        self.files = "error"

    atomic action FilesRetry:
        # The Files section's inline Retry (onRetry: the detail is read
        # again too, a poll here).
        require self.files == "error" and panel_shown(self) and still(self)
        self.files = "loading"

    # --- the composer on the home --------------------------------------

    atomic action Type:
        # Scope: the home's composer is walked before any thread.
        require self.detail == "loaded" and self.view == "home" and self.thread == "none"
        require busy_ok(self)
        require self.composer in ("empty", "failed")
        require not overlay(self) and still(self)
        if self.composer == "empty":
            self.composer = "typed"

    atomic action Send:
        # Enter (or Send): the text is trimmed non-empty and nothing is
        # in flight; a failed send's text is still there to send again.
        require self.detail == "loaded" and self.view == "home"
        require self.composer in ("typed", "failed")
        require not overlay(self) and still(self)
        self.composer = "sending"

    atomic fair action SendOk:
        # messageProject: Main() (created or reopened), Send; its orb
        # starts if it is not running. The page reloads and opens main.
        require self.composer == "sending"
        self.main = True
        if self.orb != "running":
            self.orb = "starting"
        self.composer = "empty"
        before = self.view
        self.view = "main"
        self.settle(before)

    atomic fair action SendFail:
        # Scope: only the first message, the one that creates main.
        require self.composer == "sending" and not self.main
        self.composer = "failed"

    # --- going between the home, main and the thread -----------------

    atomic action OpenMain:
        # Main's row on the home, or the column's pinned Main thread.
        require self.main and self.view != "main" and list_shown(self)
        require self.composer != "sending" and still(self) and not self.rail
        before = self.view
        self.view = "main"
        self.settle(before)

    atomic action OpenThread:
        # The thread's row; its unseen finish is acked on view. A pick in
        # the drawer leaves the drawer up (onOpen is setOpen alone).
        require self.view != "thread" and thread_row_shown(self)
        require self.composer != "sending" and still(self) and not self.rail
        before = self.view
        self.view = "thread"
        if self.thread == "unseen":
            self.thread = "done"
        self.settle(before)

    atomic action Back:
        # "< All threads" in the bar, under the scrim at tight.
        require self.detail == "loaded" and self.view != "home"
        require not overlay(self) and still(self) and not self.rail
        before = self.view
        self.view = "home"
        self.settle(before)

    # --- the thread column, its rail and its drawer --------------------

    atomic action FoldRail:
        # Scope: folded and unfolded beside one conversation (navigation
        # waits for it to be unfolded; the fold is remembered either way).
        # The column's chevron (wide only: at tight it is not drawn).
        require self.detail == "loaded" and self.view != "home" and self.wide
        require not self.rail and still(self) and self.mem == "clean"
        self.rail = True

    atomic action UnfoldRail:
        require self.detail == "loaded" and self.view != "home" and self.wide
        require self.rail and still(self)
        self.rail = False

    atomic action ToggleDone:
        # The column's Done group head.
        require self.view != "home" and column_shown(self) and self.thread == "done"
        require still(self) and self.mem == "clean"
        self.done_folded = not self.done_folded

    atomic action ToggleDrawer:
        # The bar's Threads button: drawn only beside a conversation at
        # tight. It closes the panel. With the drawer up it is under the
        # scrim, so only the panel being up leaves it clickable.
        require self.detail == "loaded" and self.view != "home" and not self.wide
        require not overlay(self) and still(self)
        self.close_panel()
        self.drawer = True

    atomic action CloseDrawer:
        # The drawer's own Close, or a tap on the scrim.
        require self.drawer and still(self)
        self.drawer = False

    # --- the Project panel ---------------------------------------------

    atomic action TogglePanel:
        # The bar's Project button. At wide the choice is remembered; at
        # tight it is a drawer and under the scrim once up, so there it
        # only opens (the panel's Close and the scrim close it). A save in
        # flight does not stop it (KNOWN GAPS 2).
        # Scope: with the composer at rest.
        require self.detail == "loaded" and not self.dialog and self.composer == "empty"
        require self.wide or (not self.panel and not self.drawer)
        if self.wide:
            if self.panel:
                self.pref = "0"
            else:
                self.pref = "1"
        if self.panel:
            self.close_panel()
        else:
            self.panel = True
        self.drawer = False

    atomic action ClosePanel:
        # The drawer's Close or the scrim: tight only.
        require panel_shown(self) and not self.wide and not self.dialog
        self.close_panel()

    atomic action Resize:
        # The viewport crosses 1080px. The confirm dialog is the
        # browser-level modal: it stays whatever happens behind it.
        # Scope: the viewport changes only on a quiet page, and the
        # tight page is walked with the thread at rest (see quiet) and
        # before the panel choice is remembered.
        require quiet(self) and not self.dialog and self.pref == ""
        self.wide = not self.wide
        self.relayout()

    # --- MEMORY.md -----------------------------------------------------

    atomic action Edit:
        require panel_shown(self) and busy_ok(self) and quiet(self)
        require self.mem in ("clean", "dirty", "failed")
        if self.mem == "clean":
            self.mem = "dirty"

    atomic action Save:
        # Enabled only with a draft that differs and no save in flight.
        require panel_shown(self) and busy_ok(self) and quiet(self)
        require self.mem in ("dirty", "failed")
        self.mem = "saving"

    atomic fair action SaveOk:
        require self.mem == "saving"
        self.mem = "saved"

    atomic fair action SaveFail:
        require self.mem == "saving"
        self.mem = "failed"

    atomic fair action SaidFades:
        require self.mem == "saved"
        self.mem = "clean"

    # --- the orb strip -------------------------------------------------

    atomic action StopOrb:
        # The strip's Stop: only while orbUp. Main has jobs running, so
        # it asks first.
        # Scope: main's orb stops only with no thread in the project.
        require panel_shown(self) and self.orb == "running" and busy_ok(self)
        require self.thread == "none" and self.composer == "empty" and self.mem == "clean"
        self.dialog = True

    atomic action ConfirmStop:
        # "Stop orb": api.stopOrb, then the page reloads.
        require self.dialog
        self.dialog = False
        self.orb = "stopped"

    atomic action CancelStop:
        # Cancel or Escape.
        require self.dialog
        self.dialog = False

    atomic fair action OrbUp:
        require self.orb == "starting"
        self.orb = "running"

    atomic action OrbExit:
        # main's owner went away: serve reports the orb stopped.
        # Not while the "saved" note is up: the page learns of it by its
        # 4 s poll, and the note is gone 2.6 s after the save.
        require self.orb == "running" and self.thread == "none"
        require self.mem != "saved"
        self.orb = "stopped"

    # --- the thread, as the 4 s poll brings it -------------------------

    atomic action StartThread:
        # Main's composer's Start thread: the thread is created running
        # and main stays on screen.
        # Scope: main hands out work while its orb runs.
        require self.view == "main" and self.main and self.thread == "none" and self.orb == "running"
        require busy_ok(self)
        require not overlay(self) and still(self)
        self.thread = "running"

    atomic action ThreadFinish:
        require self.thread == "running"
        if self.view == "thread":
            self.thread = "done"
        else:
            self.thread = "unseen"

    atomic action ThreadMessage:
        # Typing into the open thread's composer.
        require self.view == "thread" and self.thread == "done" and busy_ok(self)
        require not overlay(self) and still(self)
        self.thread = "running"

    atomic action DropOnDone:
        # Dragging an unseen thread onto Done marks it seen.
        require self.thread == "unseen" and list_shown(self) and still(self)
        self.thread = "done"

    atomic action ArchiveThread:
        # Archived or moved elsewhere (another client): it leaves the
        # list, and a page showing it goes home.
        # Scope: with the column unfolded (the rail is walked in place).
        # Not while the "saved" note is up (see OrbExit). The Done
        # group's fold is the person's and outlives the group.
        require self.thread in ("unseen", "done") and not self.rail
        require self.mem != "saved"
        self.thread = "none"
        if self.view == "thread":
            before = self.view
            self.view = "home"
            self.settle(before)

action Init:
    page = Page()

# Something always says where the page is, loading and failed included.
always assertion StatusVisible:
    return status_line(page) != ""

# Nothing but the status until the project is read: no conversation, no
# drawer, no editor state, no dialog.
always assertion NothingBeforeDetail:
    if page.detail == "loaded":
        return True
    return page.view == "home" and not page.drawer and page.mem == "clean" and not page.dialog and page.composer == "empty"

# At most one drawer covers the conversation.
always assertion OneDrawer:
    return not (page.drawer and page.panel)

# The thread drawer exists only where it is one: tight, beside a
# conversation.
always assertion DrawerOnlyWhereItIsOne:
    return not page.drawer or (not page.wide and page.view != "home")

# The middle column always has something to show: main is open only once
# it exists, the thread only while it is in the project.
always assertion OpenHasSomething:
    if page.view == "main":
        return page.main
    if page.view == "thread":
        return page.thread != "none"
    return True

# A thread on screen is never marked unseen.
always assertion UnseenNeverOnScreen:
    return not (page.view == "thread" and page.thread == "unseen")

# The composer's text and its error belong to the home.
always assertion ComposerOnHome:
    return page.composer == "empty" or page.view == "home"

# The editor holds a draft, a save or a note only while it is drawn: the
# panel is up and the files are read.
always assertion EditorNeedsPanel:
    return page.mem == "clean" or (panel_shown(page) and page.files == "loaded")

# At wide the panel is what the person last chose with the Project
# button, and unchosen it is up on the home and down beside a
# conversation, whatever happened at tight in between.
always assertion PanelFollowsChoice:
    return not page.wide or page.panel == panel_wanted(page.pref, page.view)

# The strip names a main once there is one.
always assertion StripKnowsMain:
    return page.orb == "none" or page.main

# Every request the page starts settles: a send, a save, the first read.
always eventually assertion RequestsSettle:
    return page.composer != "sending" and page.mem != "saving" and page.detail != "loading"

# KNOWN GAPS: the product as it is, modelled faithfully above; the
# property it ought to have is not asserted, since fizz fails each:
#
# 1. The strip calls a starting or building orb stopped: orbUp is false
#    until the container runs (serve sets up only for "running"), so
#    OrbLine says "Main thread's orb is stopped. It starts when you
#    message the project." right after the message that started it.
#    fizz: Init, FilesLoaded, Loaded, Type, Send, SendOk.
#      always assertion StripHonest:
#          return page.orb != "starting" or strip(page.orb, page.main) != "Main thread's orb is stopped."
#
# 2. A MEMORY.md draft is discarded without a word when the panel goes
#    down: the Project button, the scrim, a resize across 1080px, or a
#    message or a thread opened from the home (the panel default flips).
#    A save in flight then lands with nobody told. With a `dropped` flag
#    set wherever mem is reset from dirty/failed/saving, fizz fails
#    `not page.dropped` on: Init, FilesLoaded, Loaded, Edit, TogglePanel.
#
# 3. At tight, picking a thread in the drawer leaves the drawer over the
#    conversation it opened (onOpen is setOpen alone; the effect that
#    closes the drawer runs only when onThread flips). With a `picked`
#    flag, fizz: ... StartThread, ThreadFinish, DropOnDone, ToggleDone,
#    Resize, ToggleDrawer, OpenThread.
